A malformed directive on an empty declaration group reports the invalid set name, not
the emptiness: the name check runs first, so //plumb:123 gets the same diagnostic here
as anywhere else instead of hiding behind the group’s degenerate shape.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInvalidSetName
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Config struct{}

//plumb:123
const ()

//plumb:build
func NewConfig() *Config { return &Config{} }
